				<div class="post-724 post hentry category-software-reviews">
			<h2 id="post-724"><a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/index.php/2008/08/outlook-2007-does-the-little-things/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Outlook 2007 does the little things">Outlook 2007 does the little things</a></h2>
			<small class="meta">August 26th, 2008 </small>

			<div class="entry">
				<p>People give Microsoft Outlook a lot of crap, but if you&#8217;re willing to think outside the box, you&#8217;ll realize they did all the little things that make life easy.&nbsp; For instance, I rarely use the calendar popup for creating new appointments.&nbsp; No, if I have a meeting next Wednesday, I type &#8220;<em>next wed&#8221;</em> and hit tab.&nbsp; It&#8217;s at 1pm, well, type 1 and hit tab.</p>
<p>Done.</p>
